  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Big Two. Type: Climbing. Rules: 2-A-K...3 rank. Spades > Hearts > Clubs > Diamonds. Singles, Pairs, Triples, 5-card Poker hands. Goal: Empty hand.',
    Player: 'You have the 2 of Spades—the highest single in the game. An opponent just played an Ace. Regain control of the lead with your 2, then dump that troublesome pair of 4s!',
    objective: 'Be the first player to shed all cards from your hand.',
    gameplay: '1. **The Lead**: Player with 3♦ must play it (as a single or in a combo). 2. **Climbing**: Each player in turn must play a combination of the same type (single, pair, triple, or 5-card hand) that is higher in rank than the previous play. 3. **Ranks**: 2 (High) > A > K > Q ... > 3 (Low). 4. **Suits**: Spades > Hearts > Clubs > Diamonds (used to break ties in same-rank plays). 5. **Passing**: A player can pass at any time. When 3 players pass, the last player to play starts a new trick with any combo.',
    keyRules: [
      '5-card combinations must follow poker rankings: Royal Flush > Straight Flush > 4-of-a-Kind > Full House > Flush > Straight.',
      'The rank of a 5-card combo is determined by its highest card (e.g., an Ace-high Flush beats a King-high Flush).',
      'If you pass, you can still play later in the same trick cycle if the lead has not been reset.',
    ],
